A few things to note about this structure. All six motifs live inside a single `\score` block, so LilyPond produces one MIDI file. Each right-hand and left-hand staff has its own `midiChannel` assignment (channels 0 through 12, skipping channel 9 which is reserved for General MIDI percussion). The spacer rests (`s1*5/4`) offset each motif in time so they play sequentially rather than simultaneously. The `\stopStaff` and `\hideNotes` commands keep the printed layout clean — each system only shows its own motif.

The layout context removes `Timing_translator` from `Score` and adds it to each `Staff` individually, which lets each staff manage its own time signature and bar lines independently. This prevents LilyPond from complaining about mismatched durations across the staves.

The LH chords now sit at A2–C3–E3 for the A minor versions and C3–Eb3–G3 for the C minor versions, which should sound warm without being muddy.

